// One line noctalia's builtin niri template gets wrong for this session, and
// nothing else. Rendered from the live palette on every colour-scheme change
// like every other template here — see the `niri_borders` user template in
// home/joshr/niri/noctalia.nix.
//
// The builtin template draws an unfocused window's border in `surface`, which
// is the theme's background: on the dark palettes this repository ships that
// is a border you cannot see against the desktop behind it, so an unfocused
// window read as having no border at all rather than a quiet one. This says
// `on_surface_variant` instead — the same role `fg_dim` is rendered from in
// system-palette.conf, and the colour every other dimmed thing in the session
// already uses.
//
// One property, and deliberately only one. config.kdl includes this after
// noctalia.kdl, and niri merges duplicate sections property by property with
// the later definition winning, so everything else the builtin template
// renders — the active and urgent colours, the focus ring, the shadow, the
// tab indicator — is still its to decide.
layout {
    border {
        inactive-color "{{colors.on_surface_variant.default.hex}}"
    }
}
